// vue/view: a component's view as a guest document (decision 0222).
//
// The view is the one ECMAScript program main reads a `.vue` file as (`embedded: script-block`): its `<script>` and
// `<script setup>` blocks, then its template's expressions in the scopes compiler-dom gives them. Main's view
// builder writes it (vue/view.rs); the engine parses it in the dialect the scripts' `lang` names and places each of
// its nodes at the Vue construct it stands for:
//   <li v-for="item in items" :key="item.id">     view:  (items), (item) => { (item.id); };
//     guest(g, file, root, "javascript")           g is the view, parsed as JavaScript (TypeScript for lang="ts")
//     host_node(<item.id>, <the :key attribute's value>)   copied bytes: the node over them
//     host_node(<the arrow>, <the li element>)     written syntax: the construct it stands for
//
// A rule reaches the view's nodes through `guest` with the dialect named, so its kinds are that grammar's:
//   in_view(n) :- guest(g, _, _, "typescript"), docof(n, g), kind(n, "arrow_function").
// and a view node's Vue construct through host_node(n, h), the innermost `.vue` node over the bytes n stands for.

// Every component asks for its view: the embedding is the file's (its root), as main builds one per file.
embed(d, r, "script-block", "program") :- doc_role(d, "primary"), doc_root(d, r).
